For work that must change code, add a feature, fix correctness, or produce a
candidate, choose an implement workstream: `kind` "implement", `hypothesis_id`,
`title` (implementation goal), `hypothesis` (the claim to test), `task` (concrete
changes), and `pass_criteria` (observable success). Set `continue_hypothesis` to false
for a new ID and true to continue an existing one; `parent_hypothesis_id` selects its
starting candidate, and `evidence` cites measurements by location and measured revision.
A measurement applies only to the revision it measured.

Fill every free slot: a slot left free idles until a running workstream finishes.
{% if profiling %}
