`profile_id`, `target_hypothesis_id` (a listed buildable candidate, or null for the base
revision), `question` (what uncertainty to measure on that existing revision), and
`decision_impact` (which next decision depends on the answer). A profile cannot change
code or produce a candidate.
{% endif %}
Choose workstreams that investigate distinct mechanisms or competing hypotheses. Do not
split one implementation into parallel fragments and do not assign duplicate
hypothesis IDs. New IDs must not occur in the history. A continued workstream must
reuse its existing ID and set `continue_hypothesis`. Use `hypothesis_updates` to park
or abandon completed directions when evidence makes that decision clear; every update
needs `reason_kind` and a nonempty `reason`.

The framework provides isolated candidate workspaces, runs independent reviews, and
owns trusted evaluation and winner adoption. Only evaluated, accepted candidates can
be adopted or become the base revision.

